  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What is read",
      "items": [
        "Memory: router, indexes, archive, state, rules, topics and lessons; config: caps, pins and allow entries; git status/history for health.",
        "Project records: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, roadmap, shelf and brain logs/indexes. Kit: scripts/memory/KIT.json and MANIFEST.json; owned-file hashes and skill versions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where FAIL stops work",
      "items": [
        "Normal gate exits 1 on an unallowed FAIL. Checkpoint stops before commit. Memory pre-commit checks the staged snapshot with --hook --scope memory.",
        "SessionStart reports failures and always exits 0. Agents must fix or report them; the hook alone does not stop work.",
        "No-FAIL exit 0 still permits warnings. Allowed is a finding annotation, not proof that the underlying issue vanished."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope and exceptions",
      "items": [
        "Memory scope skips project record checks, while brain names remain available for resolving memory links.",
        "Allow entries need reason and date and can have ceilings. Secrets, config errors and frontmatter parse FAIL cannot be allowed. Source: engine/memory-check.mjs."
      ]
    }
  ]
